Package: tind-wireguard
Version: 0.3.2
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Morten <morten@servr.no>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: wireguard-tools, network-manager, systemd-resolved, iproute2, iputils-ping
Recommends: qrencode
Installed-Size: 72
Description: Always-on split-tunnel WireGuard to servr.no
 Per-device WireGuard enrolment for Tind. Each device generates its own key
 pair; no private key is ever shipped in the image. The tunnel only routes the
 server's own addresses (split tunnel), stays up in the background through
 NetworkManager, and resolves servr.no names through the tunnel (split DNS).
 At home it uses the server's LAN address (LAN_ENDPOINT, tried and proven on
 each network); elsewhere the endpoint name, looked up through the current
 network's DNS, never through the tunnel.
 .
 Run: sudo tind-enroll init, send the public key to the server admin, then paste the
 enrolment block that comes back into: sudo tind-enroll apply
